{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: rewrote the observational model from a loop of indexed statements `y[n] ~ normal(...)` to a single top-level protected-data sampling statement `y ~ normal(theta_obs, sigma)`. The local `theta_obs` array is a deterministic model-block helper with `theta_obs[n] = theta[indiv_idx[n]]`, so the likelihood density is unchanged. No data fields were added; `data_safe.json` is the supplied data unchanged.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;      // Number of observations
  int<lower=0> I;      // Number of components
  array[N] vector[I] y;      // Observations
  real<lower=0> sigma; // Measurement variability

  // Number of individuals in hierarchy
  int<lower=0> K;
  // Individual from which each observation is generated
  array[N] int<lower=1, upper=K> indiv_idx;
}

parameters {
  vector[I] mu;              // Population locations
  vector<lower=0>[I] tau;    // Population scales
  cholesky_factor_corr[I] L; // Population correlations
  array[K] vector[I] theta;        // Centered individual parameters
}

model {
  array[N] vector[I] theta_obs;

  mu ~ normal(0, 5);        // Prior model
  tau ~ normal(0, 5);       // Prior model
  L ~ lkj_corr_cholesky(4); // Prior model

  // Centered hierarchical model
  theta ~ multi_normal_cholesky(mu, diag_pre_multiply(tau, L));

  // Observational model
  for (n in 1:N)
    theta_obs[n] = theta[indiv_idx[n]];
  y ~ normal(theta_obs, sigma);
}

// Simulate a full observation from the current value of the parameters
generated quantities {
  array[N, I] real y_post_pred;
  for (n in 1:N)
    y_post_pred[n] = normal_rng(theta[indiv_idx[n]], sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"I":2,"K":3,"N":4,"indiv_idx":[2,2,2,2],"sigma":2.5864703643500455,"y":[[4.0,4.0],[4.0,4.0],[4.0,4.0],[4.0,3.0]]}","protected_variables":["y"]}
